      "created_at": "2011-08-21T17:56:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Apologies if this is covered elsewhere. I didn’t see such in a search.</p>\n<p>On the Atlantis card Pillars of Hercules it states:</p>\n<p>“At the start of every turn, play the top card of the villain deck”</p>\n<p>“At the start of their turn, a player may skip the rest of their turn to destroy this card”</p>\n<p>Do the above two happen simultaneously, such that the players can decide the order of them, or do they happen in the order they are on the card (, or something else)?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:40.268Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
