      "id": 21653,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-08-21T18:04:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Sounds sequential to me.  Step one is play the top card of the villain deck, step two is optionally skip turn to destroy the card.  The only “simultainious” actions I’ve ever noticed is when a reference to a number of cards greater than one is described, e.g. destroy 2 equipment cards, deal all hero targets damage, deal damage to the two targets with the highest HP, etc.  Even Slash an Burn is a sequential.  Step on, 4 melee damage to the lowest HP hero target; step two, deal 6 fire damage to the highest HP hero target.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:55:44.056Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 5101,
      "topic_slug": "pillars-of-hercules",
      "display_username": "TheJayMann",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
