      "id": 21655,
      "name": "Christopher",
      "username": "Christopher",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-08-21T18:32:09.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Those actions are, in fact, sequential, which is why they are printed on separate lines. So, even on the turn that a player chooses to skip the rest of their turn to resolve the Pillars of Hercules, the top card of the Villain deck is played.</p>\n<p>As a note, Slash and Burn used to be in the other order, but this would commonly result in one player taking 10 damage, as the highest could easily get dropped to the lowest from 6 damage.   Oooh!  A glimpse through the game-design veil!</p>",
