      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-16T17:12:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We had a bit of confusion at last night's game. Pillars of Hercules was played and Argent Adept skipped his turn to destroy it. The Adept player felt that skipping his turn meant that he could draw two cards. I felt that skipping his turn meant his turn was done so he doesn't get anything, not even an end phase. Both of those options are different than ending your turn like with Prayer of Desperation which sends you directly to the end phase.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:55:44.306Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
