      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>We had a bit of confusion at last night&#39;s game. Pillars of Hercules was played and Argent Adept skipped his turn to destroy it. The Adept player felt that skipping his turn meant that he could draw two cards. I felt that skipping his turn meant his turn was done so he doesn&#39;t get anything, not even an end phase. Both of those options are different than ending your turn like with Prayer of Desperation which sends you directly to the end phase.</p>",
