      "id": 21663,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-16T19:39:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If you skip your turn, this occurs during your Start phase, so you'd still get to do any actions that'd trigger during that phase (yay for Omni-10 :D). But you'd skip everything else in your turn. Anything which specifies to <span class=\"bbcode-i\">end</span> your turn means you skip straight to the End phase (so can't play a card, use a power, or draw any cards), though not many characters have any possible actions during that phase. Double-drawing due to not playing a card or using a power is done during your Draw phase - if you've skipped your turn, you don't <span class=\"bbcode-i\">get</span> a Draw phase. Also, drawing during your Draw phase is never mandatory, just as you don't have to play a card or use a power. Just in case you weren't aware of that - sometimes, drawing cards can be rather painful (eg of Apostate has his Tome out).</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
